# Pins the OTHER half of the parse-error contract that malformed.ttl cannot
# reach on its own: a syntax error partway through a graph must not discard
# the triples already parsed before it. One complete, valid triple appears
# first (sd:feature sd:UnionDefaultGraph), then a second statement breaks on
# an unterminated IRI. A naive implementation that throws the whole graph
# away on any error would report triples == 0 and an empty `features` set
# here -- identical to malformed.ttl's expected output -- which is exactly
# the regression this fixture exists to catch.
@prefix sd: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sparql-service-description#> .

<http://example.org/sparql> sd:feature sd:UnionDefaultGraph .

<http://example.org/sparql
    sd:feature sd:DereferencesURIs .
